msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-antenna-design.rst:244
#: 31a9f07d5d4b4247ab6ed76429fea5b2
msgid "The ratio of diameters D/d is chosen to give the desired impedance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-antenna-design.rst:247
#: 388c15cc8f5e4d719f4915fb62342315
msgid "D/d = 1.86 for 75ohms, and 1.5 for 50 ohms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-antenna-design.rst:248
#: 9a3799e25ad44c118780229b60c4f8a7
msgid "Typically the outer tube would be around 8mm for use at 2.4GHz."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-antenna-design.rst:249
#: 37eb5f968bb9449e9203b177d1b2f915
msgid "In order to obtain circular polarisation, I mentioned that the two dipole have to be fed 90deg apart ( phase quadrature)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-antenna-design.rst:251
#: 17cb54f54430440eaa0a1246acde551e
msgid "This can be done as in the coax balun version above ( inserting an extra 1/4wave length of coax in the leg to one dipole gives an extra electrical wavelegnth of 90 degerees)."
